.TH NYX-PINGSWEEP 8 "2025" "NYX Framework" "NYX Phobos Tools"
.SH NAME
nyx-pingsweep \- ICMP network discovery tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nyx-pingsweep
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nyx-pingsweep
performs ICMP-based network discovery by sending Echo Requests to
every host in a given CIDR range. It identifies which hosts are
alive and reports their round-trip latency.
.PP
When launched, it enters an interactive shell with line editing,
tab completion, and command history. Type
.B help
for available commands.
.PP
Scanning is performed in parallel using a configurable number of
threads to minimise total sweep time.
.SH INTERACTIVE COMMANDS
.TP
.BI scan " -c cidr" " [-i iface]" " [-t ms]" " [-T N]"
Run ICMP ping sweep on a CIDR range. Options:
.RS
.TP
.BI \-c " cidr" "\fR, \fP" \-\-cidr " cidr"
Target subnet in CIDR notation (required).
.TP
.BI \-i " iface" "\fR, \fP" \-\-interface " iface"
Network interface to use. Auto-detected if omitted.
.TP
.BI \-t " ms" "\fR, \fP" \-\-timeout " ms"
Timeout per host in milliseconds. Default is 1000.
.TP
.BI \-T " n" "\fR, \fP" \-\-threads " n"
Number of scanning threads. Default is 32.
.RE
.TP
.B list
List available network interfaces with MAC, IP, and status.
.TP
.B help
Show available commands and usage.
.TP
.B exit
Exit the shell.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
sudo nyx-pingsweep
pingsweep> scan -c 192.168.1.0/24
pingsweep> scan -c 10.0.0.0/24 -T 8 -t 500
pingsweep> list
pingsweep> exit
.fi
.SH NOTES
This tool requires root privileges (raw ICMP sockets). When launched
without root from a terminal, it will attempt to re-execute itself
with sudo.
